                        ],
                        "form": "Moortjes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e9d2275-ee37-3783-8407-5b7a15562dc2",
                        "entry_id": "95c2800f-13e2-3f7f-87ba-f21b2710632b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "moslim, met name in Noord-Afrika en het Iberisch schiereiland, heel vaak in"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a34cb7d0-f664-4339-9d37-ae55ffe824c9",
                                "sense_id": "8e9d2275-ee37-3783-8407-5b7a15562dc2",
                                "text": "Die vierde es coninc van den Moren,[En̄ e]s gheheten die coninc Genors; [Die] .v.ste dat es die coninc Anfors, [En̄ e]s coninc in Getulen [Daer d]e[r] liebaerde vele sculen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae0a6e3a-476d-47c1-9d07-cc868862b1c3",
                                "sense_id": "8e9d2275-ee37-3783-8407-5b7a15562dc2",
                                "text": "Ende ten lesten heeft hi Abdelle, coninc der Moren, weder thuijs ghesent doer zijn soon Lodewijc ende andere princen, ende heeften gheeert ende begavet mit coninclike cleinoden ende costelike presenten ende gaven."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "08256a75-3356-39f0-b061-b61b7ab6de5b",
                        "entry_id": "95c2800f-13e2-3f7f-87ba-f21b2710632b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "donkere Afrikaan (vaak gekwalificeerd met bijvoeglijk swart)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a6eadcb-50cc-49ce-9e44-38c07a4fc5eb",
                                "sense_id": "08256a75-3356-39f0-b061-b61b7ab6de5b",
                                "text": "Was een coninghinne daerbi In Etyopen, hiet Candacis, Daer menech swart moor in is, Die sinde up minne ende up houde Van utermaten finen goude Alexandere hondert sticke Voets lanc ende voets dicke Ende enen halven voet breet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1bc8ba98-76c1-475f-89a2-b0c9724aee9a",
                                "sense_id": "08256a75-3356-39f0-b061-b61b7ab6de5b",
                                "text": "Het veel hoofdige Elck is over al geboren, Ellick leeft hier en daer, elck is verr' ende hent, Elck schuylt in 't Nederlandt, en by de swarte Moren, En ellick woont in elck, maer ellick onbekent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b4e4aedd-d67e-4bcb-9ae9-95f666d18b30",
                        "source_entry_id": "95c2800f-13e2-3f7f-87ba-f21b2710632b",
                        "target_lang_word": "mauritanian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fd89a684-7337-4772-9479-92eadfca5860",
                        "source_entry_id": "95c2800f-13e2-3f7f-87ba-f21b2710632b",
                        "target_lang_word": "moor",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "moor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "16adb73e-82b5-3372-8d30-b6ea7af80548",
                                        "entry_id": "158475b2-fb51-3fea-a711-8d4f8c02b8b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An extensive waste covered with patches of heath, and having a poor, light (and usually acidic) soil, but sometimes marshy, and abounding in peat; a heath. (Compare bog, peatland, marsh, swamp, fen.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e30a2270-9abb-4763-aaea-d941f6892508",
                                                "sense_id": "16adb73e-82b5-3372-8d30-b6ea7af80548",
                                                "text": "A cold, biting wind blew across the moor, and the travellers hastened their step."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "027f8fe0-72f2-4fd8-831b-291ace218a24",
                                                "sense_id": "16adb73e-82b5-3372-8d30-b6ea7af80548",
                                                "text": "In her girlish age, she kept sheep on the moor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c96aa813-4514-4317-8e2f-cf74a23dad9b",
                                                "sense_id": "16adb73e-82b5-3372-8d30-b6ea7af80548",
                                                "text": "the ruins yet resting in the wild moors"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e4298a5-080c-4cf5-9a6b-f7c5817a8ffd",
                                                "sense_id": "16adb73e-82b5-3372-8d30-b6ea7af80548",
                                                "text": "And now, without a word of warning from the Ghost, they stood upon a bleak and desert moor, where monstrous masses of rude stone were cast about, as though it were the burial-place of giants; and water spread itself wheresoever it listed, or would have done so, but for the frost that held it prisoner; and nothing grew but moss and furze, and coarse rank grass."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "319263a1-b5d4-32df-84b2-a0f7a001be25",
                                        "entry_id": "158475b2-fb51-3fea-a711-8d4f8c02b8b9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A game preserve consisting of moorland."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "moor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ed86d486-d24b-3b9b-a2f0-ca276e514be6",
                                        "entry_id": "d185793e-512e-3be6-b5e3-3490d41d7f6a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cast anchor or become fastened."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54fb8268-ba4b-4551-9a4f-14411d41a881",
                                                "sense_id": "ed86d486-d24b-3b9b-a2f0-ca276e514be6",
                                                "text": "The vessel moored in the stream."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d489cb55-5e38-3d42-9720-3e0a78905aaa",
                                        "entry_id": "d185793e-512e-3be6-b5e3-3490d41d7f6a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fix or secure (e.g. a vessel) in a particular place by casting anchor, or by fastening with ropes, cables or chains or the like."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "56b96907-cc44-4cea-971c-4d05dee26084",
                                                "sense_id": "d489cb55-5e38-3d42-9720-3e0a78905aaa",
                                                "text": "They moored the boat to the wharf."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66c898bd-9efd-4006-80a8-5a54f2d11b9d",
                                                "sense_id": "d489cb55-5e38-3d42-9720-3e0a78905aaa",
                                                "text": "His thought is tied, the curving prow\nOf motion moored to rock;\nAnd minutes burst upon a brow\nInsentient to shock."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f96558e-f91e-3b08-a277-d8ee94e23508",
                                        "entry_id": "d185793e-512e-3be6-b5e3-3490d41d7f6a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To secure or fix firmly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
